{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>These are the heads of their fathers' houses.</b> Since the end of Israel's term had arrived for redemption and they were now about to be separated from among the Egyptians, Scripture traced their lineage and prefaced with the word אלה in order to separate off the Egyptians. He began with Reuben, for he was the firstborn, and traced the lineage through Levi. The intent in this was to mention the two redeemers, Moses and Aaron, who are from the tribe of Levi; for had he begun with 'these are the names of the sons of Levi,' it would have appeared that Levi was the first in the genealogy. For the honor of Moses he did thus, and therefore he began from Reuben and went on mentioning until Levi the third."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:56:29.593681340Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}